e — without waking the service behind it —\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text directly states the claim with equivalent wording.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-003\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Requests are counted against the credential that presented them,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this explicitly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-004\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"over a fixed window of 60 seconds,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states the window duration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-005\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"never against a connection.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states requests are never counted against a connection.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-006\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Opening a second socket therefore buys a caller nothing,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text uses identical wording for this claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-007\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a client spread across multiple worker processes is throttled at exactly the point a single process would have been.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text supports the principle but specifies 'multiple' processes, not the specific number 'eight.'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-008\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text does not mention any cost associated with extra file descriptors.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-009\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states this exactly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-010\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states the batch allowance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-011\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A refusal is not an outage,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states this claim directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-012\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Callers that retry immediately are the largest single reason the cap is there at all.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"'Immediately' and 'at once' convey the same meaning in this context.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-013\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The refusal carries a Retry-After header.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states this explicitly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-014\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Its value is a whole number of seconds to wait.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly describes the header value format.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-015\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Waiting that long and then continuing is the whole of the contract —\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states this exactly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-016\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this claim directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-017\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"waiting longer than the header asks earns a caller no credit at all.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text uses equivalent wording for this claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-018\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The body of the refusal is JSON,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states the body format.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-019\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"It names what the gateway calls the \\\"window\\\" it counted in.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states what the body contains.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-020\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"It names the cap and the tier as well.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states the body names these fields.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-021\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"None of those fields is a substitute for the header,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states this claim directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-022\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a caller that parses the body to compute its own wait is doing the same arithmetic twice.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text uses identical wording.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-023\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states this claim directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-024\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and it does the same on the 503 path.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states this.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-025\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A wait derived on the client side is a guess about a counter it cannot see.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this exactly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-026\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A 200 wants nothing,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text uses identical wording.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-027\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a 429 wants the stated wait,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-028\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"'May be retried' and 'can be retried' convey the same meaning.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-029\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and a 503 is the overload path.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states this claim directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-030\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The four cases are not interchangeable.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this explicitly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-031\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A client that folds every non-success into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text uses this claim word-for-word.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-032\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-033\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and it is measured over exactly the same window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states the batch window.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-034\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The tier is set on the credential when it is issued\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-035\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and cannot be asked for per call.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text directly states this.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-036\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this exactly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-037\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A caller that cannot say how often it was refused last week cannot argue for a larger cap,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states this claim directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-038\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and nobody at the far end will assemble that argument on its behalf.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text uses equivalent wording for this claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-039\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The log line should carry the credential, the window and the wait.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states this exactly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-040\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states the number of refusal reasons.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-041\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and only one of them is the one above.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states that the rate cap is one of the three reasons.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-042\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A credential may be suspended,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly lists this as a refusal reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-043\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a route may be closed for maintenance,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states this as a refusal reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-044\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly lists this as a refusal reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-045\",\n    