rdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Four rules, given in the order they should be applied.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states there are four rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-016\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and it does the same on the 503 path.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text directly states the gateway applies the same arithmetic principle to 503.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-017\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text lists safe-to-retry cases but does not explicitly compare set sizes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-018\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A 200 wants nothing,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"'Needs' and 'wants' are equivalent in this context.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-019\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a 429 wants the stated wait,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text uses equivalent wording.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-020\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"'Can be retried' and 'may be retried' convey the same meaning.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-021\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a 503 is the overload path.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"'Overload path' necessarily means the platform is overloaded when 503 is returned.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-022\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states the batch allowance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-023\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"1000 is 10 times the default (100), not 50 times.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-024\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and it is measured over exactly the same window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Identical window and measurement method mean the same counting scheme is used.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-025\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"'Nothing else differs' necessarily entails window, header, and body are identical.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-026\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text directly states no other differences between batch and default tiers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-027\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states three separate refusal reasons.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-028\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and only one of them is the one above.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states the rate cap is the only cap-related reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-029\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"These two reasons don't involve current-window traffic counts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-030\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A credential may be suspended,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly lists this refusal reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-031\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a route may be closed for maintenance,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Maintenance includes repair.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-032\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text lists body size as a refusal reason but does not specify timing of refusal or whether the body is read.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-033\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"'Burns its whole budget' and 'spends its whole budget' convey the same meaning; 'reaches nothing' means never reaching the service.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-034\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and the log afterwards shows nothing at all except a long run of refusals.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"'Nothing except refusals' entails no successes and only refusals.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-035\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states the budget is spent but does not specify it is the caller's own budget or that they bear the cost.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-036\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A cap can be raised,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this explicitly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-037\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A cap can be raised, but only with measurement.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"'Only with measurement' necessarily entails no raises without measurement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-038\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty — a burst is cheaper to smooth than it is to serve at its peak. A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text indicates smoothness is evaluated before changing the cap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-039\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel,\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-040\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"There is no expedited path\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states this.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-041\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"evidence\": \"they are answered within two working days.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states 'within' two days, not exactly two days; the claim is slightly more specific.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-042\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"There is no expedited path\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No expedited path necessarily means chasing the request cannot make it faster.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":114896,"type":"result","duration_ms":164791,"uuid":"6aba9336-a119-48dc-bd66-56be50fecad3","ttft_stream_ms":3076,"time_to_request_ms":1872,"first_content_frame_ms":3076,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
